# Every text file checks out with LF, on every machine. Without this line a
# clone on a host with core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) gets CRLF in
# SKILL.md and the .mjs files, and the checkout no longer matches what was
# committed. That is not cosmetic here: the tests parse SKILL.md with patterns
# written for LF, and the preview page's byte-identity check compares committed
# bytes. Found when tests/docs.mjs died on a Windows clone — and it reproduced
# on an unmodified checkout, so it was the repo's to fix, not that machine's.
# The rules below deliberately override this one; later rules win.
* text=auto eol=lf

# core.bundle.js is a minified build artefact with a base64 payload on one line,
# and Windows clones default to autocrlf. Marking these binary keeps a checkout
# byte-identical to what was committed, which the preview page's byte-identity
# check depends on.
src/core.bundle.js binary
*.png binary

# Templates become C# and markdown in someone's project; leave the endings alone.
templates/* -text
